"Line 18 is the \u0060DiscountRates[order.DiscountCode]\u0060 lookup, and \u0060SUMMER25\u0060 does not appear anywhere in the repo. I\u0027ll check the callers and any tests for this method.The cause is in the code, and I\u0027m confident about it. I changed no files.\n\n**Line 18 is the failing lookup.** \u0060src/OrderService/Api/OrderTotal.cs\u0060 line 18 is \u0060decimal rate = DiscountRates[order.DiscountCode];\u0060. The \u0060DiscountRates\u0060 table holds only \u0060WELCOME10\u0060 (0.10) and \u0060VIP20\u0060 (0.20). When an order carries \u0060SUMMER25\u0060, the indexer throws \u0060KeyNotFoundException\u0060. That matches the stack trace and the runbook\u0027s note that marketing retires codes without telling engineering.\n\n**\u0060SUMMER25\u0060 is not in the repository.** Searching the whole order-service folder finds no mention of it. So the code is not wrong about that code. It is the data side: order 1003 carries a code that is no longer in the table. I did not open the order store, so I haven\u0027t seen order 1003\u0027s record directly. The error\u0027s key name is the only evidence that it holds \u0060SUMMER25\u0060.\n\n**The proposed fix leaves the other totals unchanged.** Replacing the indexer with a \u0060TryGetValue\u0060 that falls back to a rate of 0 would not change these totals:\n- **WELCOME10 and VIP20:** the table still returns the same rates, so the formula \u0060Math.Round(subtotal * (1 - rate), 2)\u0060 gives the same result.\n- **No code:** the early return \u0060if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(order.DiscountCode)) return subtotal;\u0060 runs before the lookup, so nothing changes.\n\nThe existing tests in \u0060tests/OrderService.Tests/OrderApiTests.cs\u0060 cover the no-discount case (order 1002 \u2192 899.00) and the discount case (order 1001 \u2192 26.10). Those are the checks that should still pass after the fix. I did not run them.\n\n**Decision inputs for the manager:**\n- Area: **code**. The method crashes on a code the runbook says must give no discount.\n- Confidence: **high**. I can point at the line and say what it should do.\n- Caveat: the fix would give order 1003 its full subtotal, which is what the runbook asks for. Whether that is the right business answer for a retired promotion is not something I can judge.\n\n[Answered by triage.investigator, did: ReadWorkspaceFile: namespace OrderService;; SearchWorkspace: No matches found.; SearchWorkspace: demos/louis-agent/samples/order-service/src/OrderService/Api/OrderTotal.cs:7: [\u2026; SearchWorkspace: demos/louis-agent/samples/order-service/tests/OrderService.Tests/OrderApiTests.\u2026; SearchWorkspace: demos/louis-agent/samples/order-service/tests/OrderService.Tests/OrderApiTests.\u2026; ReportInvestigation: Recorded step 2 of run eval-order-total-1003-20261127-060003-triage-1: The inve\u2026]"